.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 13, 2026
.Dt NEWFS_OXFS 8
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm newfs_oxfs
.Nd make an oxfs file system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl N
.Op Fl L Ar volname
.Op Fl i Ar bytes
.Op Fl s Ar size
.Ar special
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
makes an empty oxfs file system on
.Ar special ,
a raw disk partition such as
.Pa /dev/virt0p2
or an image file.
The kernel never formats a file system itself.
.Pp
The file system covers all of
.Ar special .
A disk device's size comes from its
.Dv DIOCGMEDIASIZE
.Xr ioctl 2 ,
an image file's from its length.
The new file system holds the root directory and
.Pa /lost+found
(mode 0700), where
.Xr fsck_oxfs 8
reconnects files that lose their names, and is marked clean.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl N
Print the layout the file system would have, and write nothing.
.It Fl L Ar volname
Give the file system a volume label of up to 32 letters, digits,
.Ql - ,
.Ql _
and
.Ql \&. .
.It Fl i Ar bytes
Make one inode for every
.Ar bytes
of the file system up front.
oxfs adds inodes as files need them, a block of 32 at a time, so without
.Fl i
only the first block of them is made.
.It Fl s Ar size
Use only the first
.Ar size
512-byte sectors of
.Ar special .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fsck_oxfs 8 ,
.Xr mount 8
.Sh BUGS
A disk device that holds the root file system mounted read-write can't be
written, so
.Nm
can't format it then.
